<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of the Hwicce</h1><p class="st-meta">577 CE – 780 CE (approx.) · capital Worcester</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An Anglo-Saxon sub-kingdom of the lower Severn valley around Worcester, ruled by its own kings under Mercian overlordship.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Hwicce took shape in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gloucestershire">Gloucestershire</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/worcestershire">Worcestershire</a> and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warwickshire">Warwickshire</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">West Saxon</a> victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dyrham">Dyrham</a> in 577 opened the region to English settlement. By the 7th century the area was ruled by a local dynasty, possibly installed or confirmed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penda-of-mercia">Penda</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-mercia">Kingdom of Mercia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Hwiccan kings such as Osric and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oshere">Oshere</a> endowed early minsters, Osric being credited with founding those at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bath">Bath</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gloucester">Gloucester</a>, and a bishopric was created at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/worcester">Worcester</a> around 680 to serve the people. The territory was rich in salt from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/droitwich-spa">Droitwich</a> and in farmland, and its charters are among the earliest English documents.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Hwiccan rulers were downgraded from kings to ealdormen in the late 8th century under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/offa-of-mercia">Offa</a>. The kingdom's boundaries survived as the medieval diocese of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/worcester">Worcester</a>, preserving its outline for centuries.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-the-hwicce.jpg" alt="Kingdom of the Hwicce" width="320" height="391"><figcaption>Image: ðarkuncoll · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hwicce_kingdom.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>577 CE – 780 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Worcester</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Osric, Oshere</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>United Kingdom</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hwicce</dd></dl></aside></div>
